# Omnuv's own QML directory declaration.
#
# **Without this file nothing of ours draws, and nothing says why.**
# `Theme.qml` is `pragma Singleton`, and a singleton is only a type if
# something declares it: a `qmldir` beside it, or `qmlRegisterSingletonType`
# from C++. There was neither. So `Theme` resolved to nothing, every file
# saying `Theme.` failed to compile, and the view that pushes them reported
#
#     QQmlComponent: Component is not ready
#     qrc:/gui/main.qml:149:5: QML StackView: push:
#         qrc:/omnuv/OmnuvView.qml:620:5: Type StreamSettingsSheet unavailable
#
# — which names the leaf rather than the cause, and leaves a blank white
# window behind it. Four of the five QML files here use `Theme.`, so that was
# the whole of our interface.
#
# It was invisible to everything that was checking: the build is green, the
# process runs, the tray works, `style=FluentWinUI3` is genuinely what drew,
# and thirty-five assertions in `lab-windows-build.yml` passed — because all
# of them read the application's log for properties and none of them asked
# whether anything was on the screen. A screenshot is what found it.
# **No `module` line on purpose.** Naming a module here would make this an
# installed module that has to be found on an import path; what is wanted is
# the implicit import every QML file gets of its own directory, which reads
# this file and nothing else.
singleton Theme 1.0 Theme.qml
